<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Cleopatra returns at 11 weeks 0 days by her last period. This morning&apos;s ultrasound with Dr. Haddad-Thornbury of maternal-fetal medicine showed two live fetuses with a thick dividing membrane and a twin-peak sign: a dichorionic diamniotic twin pregnancy. The crown-rump lengths (45 and 46 mm) agree with her dates within three days, so her due date is unchanged. There are no fibroids and no features of a molar pregnancy. The nausea has eased on doxylamine with pyridoxine; she vomits about once a day and keeps food and fluids down (PUQE 7). She takes the prenatal vitamin and ferrous sulfate every other day. She has had no bleeding or pain. She was surprised by the news of twins and is pleased, though she is already thinking about how she will manage her work. Her first-visit results are back. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ultrasound</td><td>Dichorionic diamniotic twins; dates confirmed; no fibroids or molar features</td></tr><tr><td>Nausea</td><td>Easing; vomits about once a day; PUQE 7</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Prenatal vitamin, ferrous sulfate every other day, doxylamine with pyridoxine at bedtime</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>No bleeding or pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

